IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Diplomatic and Consular Missions Act 1978 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND
-- THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01897.txt.
-- The person displaying a sign or making a claim asks: "Is my conduct caught;
-- can I be restrained by injunction; can my sign be taken down, and for how
-- long can a warrant run?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 4(1)(a): the mission whose status the conduct concerns.
DECLARE `Mission concerned` IS ONE OF
    `a diplomatic or consular mission of a country, established in Australia with the Commonwealth's consent`
    `a designated overseas mission of a foreign territory`
    `no such mission`

-- s 4(2)(a)-(b), (2A), (2B).
DECLARE `Conduct` IS ONE OF
    `displaying a sign, flag or insignia, or causing or permitting it`
    `making or publishing a representation, or causing or permitting it`

DECLARE `Missions case` HAS
    `the mission concerned`                                         IS A `Mission concerned`
    `my conduct`                                                    IS A `Conduct`
    -- s 4(2)(a), (2A)(c): premises of the mission or a member's residence
    `the premises are the mission's office or a member's residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(2)(a)-(b), (2A)(d), (2B)(b): what the sign or representation states,
    -- implies or is reasonably capable of being taken to imply
    `it implies another mission representing that country or territory` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(2)(c)-(d)
    `I act for a designated overseas mission in an authorised capacity, or at its staff's request` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(2A)(e), (2B)(c)
    `I act for a consented diplomatic or consular mission in that capacity, or at a member's request` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(5)-(6): the Court's findings
    `the Court is satisfied I have engaged in it`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it appears to the Court I am likely to engage in it`           IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 5(5)
    `a removal warrant was issued on`                               IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `Missions position` HAS
    `my conduct is caught by section 4`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `an injunction may be granted against me`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `a warrant to remove my sign may issue`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day a removal warrant can be in force`                IS A MAYBE DATE

§ `Rules`

-- s 4(2) (a consented mission of a country), (2A) and (2B) (a designated
-- overseas mission of a foreign territory).
@ref s 4(2), (2A), (2B)
GIVEN c IS A `Missions case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my conduct is caught` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `the mission concerned`
    WHEN `a diplomatic or consular mission of a country, established in Australia with the Commonwealth's consent` THEN
            `the conduct itself is caught` c
        AND NOT (c's `I act for a designated overseas mission in an authorised capacity, or at its staff's request`)
    WHEN `a designated overseas mission of a foreign territory` THEN
            `the conduct itself is caught` c
        AND NOT (c's `I act for a consented diplomatic or consular mission in that capacity, or at a member's request`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 4(2)(a), (2A)(a)-(d): a sign at premises that are not the mission's office
-- or a member's residence; s 4(2)(b), (2B)(a)-(b): a representation.
@ref s 4(2)(a)-(b), (2A)(a)-(d), (2B)(a)-(b)
GIVEN c IS A `Missions case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct itself is caught` c IF
        c's `it implies another mission representing that country or territory`
    AND (   c's `my conduct` EQUALS `making or publishing a representation, or causing or permitting it`
         OR NOT (c's `the premises are the mission's office or a member's residence`))

-- s 4(1), (5)(a), (6)(a): on the Attorney-General's application, if the Court
-- is satisfied I have engaged in it, or it appears I am likely to.
@ref s 4(1), (5)-(6)
GIVEN c IS A `Missions case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an injunction may be granted` c IF
        `my conduct is caught` c
    AND (c's `the Court is satisfied I have engaged in it` OR c's `it appears to the Court I am likely to engage in it`)

-- s 5(1): where the Court has found that displaying a sign is caught.
@ref s 5(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Missions case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a removal warrant may issue` c IF
        `my conduct is caught` c
    AND c's `my conduct` EQUALS `displaying a sign, flag or insignia, or causing or permitting it`
    AND c's `the Court is satisfied I have engaged in it`

-- s 5(5): "a period not exceeding 6 months", taken as beginning on the day of
-- issue: it ends on the day before the corresponding day 6 months later, or
-- at the end of that month where it has no corresponding day.
@ref s 5(5)
GIVEN c IS A `Missions case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of a removal warrant` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `a removal warrant was issued on`
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (`the end of 6 months beginning with` d)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of 6 months beginning with` d MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY (`add months` d 6) LESS THAN DATE_DAY d
    THEN `add months` d 6
    ELSE `the day before` (`add months` d 6)

@ref ss 4-5
@export default The position of a person who displays a sign, flag or insignia, or makes a representation, implying a diplomatic or consular office or residence in Australia, under the Diplomatic and Consular Missions Act 1978 (Cth): whether the conduct is caught by s 4 (for a mission established with the Commonwealth's consent, or a designated overseas mission of a foreign territory, with the exceptions for those acting for such missions); whether the Federal Court may grant an injunction on the Attorney-General's application (if satisfied I have engaged in it, or that I am likely to); whether a warrant may issue to remove my sign (s 5); and the last day such a warrant can be in force (at most 6 months). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Missions case`  @desc The mission concerned, my conduct and what it implies, any capacity I act in, the Court's findings, and any warrant
GIVETH A `Missions position`
`the missions position for` c MEANS
    `Missions position` OF `my conduct is caught` c, `an injunction may be granted` c, `a removal warrant may issue` c, `the last day of a removal warrant` c
